  "worked_solution": "Our goal is to express $V$ in terms of $h.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $r$ in the above equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =5 \\\\ r & =5h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $r=5h$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\pi (5h)^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 25{h}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =25\\pi {h}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
